WEBVTT

00:01.880 --> 00:07.500
This year, my mom left the big production company and
became the president of her very own company.

00:08.000 --> 00:12.710
I love how my mom is so cool and good at her job.

00:13.040 --> 00:17.080
That's why I want to be just like my mom someday.

00:14.290 --> 00:16.040
She really is so weird.

00:16.040 --> 00:17.080
I know.

00:17.710 --> 00:20.130
Class 6-2, Kano Hayakawa.

00:20.880 --> 00:22.880
Uhh... Kano?

00:22.880 --> 00:23.330
Yes?

00:23.330 --> 00:31.290
<b>Future
Dreams</b>

00:23.710 --> 00:26.670
Today's essay was supposed
to be on your future dreams.

00:27.040 --> 00:31.330
I know! My dream is to grow up to be like my mom!

00:40.250 --> 00:45.170
When will I be able to use magic?

00:45.290 --> 00:50.040
I've always longed for something special

00:50.330 --> 00:55.210
1, 2, 3, fall in line, B, C, D, eagerly obedient

00:55.330 --> 01:00.790
But I know best, that that's not me

01:01.670 --> 01:07.420
No one thinks this is ok the way it is

01:07.420 --> 01:10.210
Anxious legs weighing me down

01:11.210 --> 01:14.880
Even you, who I hold so close

01:15.000 --> 01:19.580
Being frustratingly out of reach, what I see is...

01:19.830 --> 01:25.460
A variety of colors, a myriad of brightness

01:25.460 --> 01:30.460
Even if I've been fed up countless times -resonating with you-

01:30.670 --> 01:35.420
Breaking through my thoughts that seem to be on a loop

01:35.420 --> 01:40.040
Mayday to these melancholic days, I dance in the air

01:40.040 --> 01:44.750
Taking a bite out of the gloomy sky

01:44.920 --> 01:52.710
There's an unexpected sweetness, amidst the bitter, sour, salty taste

01:55.040 --> 02:01.790
I'm moving towards where the light shines

02:10.170 --> 02:13.580
<b>Episode 9:   Take a Look at Reality</b>

02:12.460 --> 02:13.130
<b>Followers</b>

02:13.330 --> 02:14.710
Wow!

02:15.210 --> 02:16.040
We did it!

02:16.040 --> 02:17.790
100k followers!

02:17.790 --> 02:19.420
We achieved our goal!

02:19.630 --> 02:20.540
We did, huh?

02:21.250 --> 02:22.710
You're surprisingly calm.

02:22.710 --> 02:23.290
Huh?

02:23.500 --> 02:26.330
True, I thought you might be more overjoyed.

02:27.420 --> 02:29.210
Now that you mention it.

02:29.460 --> 02:31.250
Well, I think it's a good thing.

02:31.710 --> 02:36.960
It means you're not fixated on just goals or
the number of followers, and you're relaxing a bit.

02:36.960 --> 02:39.880
Yeah, and I realized something, too.

02:40.250 --> 02:41.170
Realized something?

02:42.380 --> 02:47.830
More than us getting popular, it's much more important
that I get to sing as a part of JELEE.

02:48.420 --> 02:49.460
Nono-tan!

02:51.170 --> 02:54.460
I'm so glad I decided to follow you, Nono-tan.

02:54.460 --> 02:58.210
What's our next goal, then?!
I shall accompany you to the ends of hell!

02:58.210 --> 02:59.710
Why hell?

03:02.380 --> 03:03.960
A goal, huh?

03:07.040 --> 03:09.170
Hey, what do you want to do, Mahiru?

03:09.330 --> 03:10.630
Uh, me?!

03:11.250 --> 03:13.630
Hmm, a goal...

03:15.000 --> 03:18.210
I want to get better at drawing... I guess?

03:18.750 --> 03:20.960
Well, that's a goal for you, though.

03:20.960 --> 03:22.540
Huh, you're right.

03:22.540 --> 03:24.210
Oh, come on!

03:25.790 --> 03:26.920
What?

03:26.920 --> 03:30.580
A New Year's Eve Virtual Live
Gig Event at Miyashita Park?

03:27.960 --> 03:30.880
<b>Sunflower Dolls
New Year's Eve Virtual Live Gig Event
Proposal</b>

03:31.170 --> 03:33.080
That's a really major job.

03:33.580 --> 03:35.170
Way out of your league.

03:36.040 --> 03:37.170
I know, right?

03:37.460 --> 03:38.750
Do you want to take it on?

03:39.210 --> 03:40.920
Honestly, I'm scared.

03:41.210 --> 03:42.830
Always the scaredy-cat, huh Mahi-

03:42.830 --> 03:44.880
But I'm kinda intrigued.

03:46.830 --> 03:50.750
I mean, I always thought I was
a jellyfish that couldn't swim,

03:51.040 --> 03:56.080
but once I dove into new waters,
I gradually started to like my art.

03:57.420 --> 03:59.250
So I'm conflicted.

03:59.580 --> 04:03.130
If I take on this job, I feel like I'll find more
confidence in myself.

04:04.290 --> 04:09.000
If I pass up this opportunity,
I probably won't get another chance like this, will I?

04:10.460 --> 04:11.250
Well...

04:11.750 --> 04:12.960
Most definitely not!

04:12.960 --> 04:15.080
Hey! Stop laying on the pressure!

04:18.130 --> 04:20.130
And what will Kano think?

04:20.920 --> 04:22.460
Yeah, I know right?

04:22.960 --> 04:26.460
I promised we'd make a music video
by the end of the year, too.

04:27.000 --> 04:27.580
That, and...

04:28.130 --> 04:29.080
Mommy!

04:30.750 --> 04:33.920
Her relationship with her mother, right?

04:31.040 --> 04:31.960
Pick me up!

04:34.290 --> 04:35.040
Yeah.

04:35.040 --> 04:36.500
Whee, I'm so high up!

04:38.500 --> 04:41.500
Well, I figure she'll understand if you talk to her about it.

04:42.580 --> 04:43.830
You think so...?

04:44.170 --> 04:46.250
Yeah. Besides, y'know...

04:47.000 --> 04:49.460
Your life is yours to choose, right Mahiru?

04:50.500 --> 04:53.750
You want to know about Nono-tan's
mother Yukine Hayakawa?

04:53.750 --> 04:55.960
<b>Sunflower Dolls</b>

04:54.750 --> 04:56.000
Y-yeah.

04:56.250 --> 04:57.790
Why the sudden interest, though?

04:58.250 --> 05:00.630
Well, there's a bunch of reasons, I guess.

05:01.250 --> 05:05.250
Oh, of course. Everyone has their reasons, I suppose.

05:05.670 --> 05:08.330
These are the times when I'm glad
she takes things at face value.

05:08.790 --> 05:11.210
Then I'll give you a brief explanation.

05:14.580 --> 05:20.710
And so! Ms. Yukine Hayakawa is the very genius
who unearthed Nono-tan's talents,

05:20.710 --> 05:23.210
and the greatest strategist this century has known!

05:23.540 --> 05:26.880
Thanks, that was about ten times
as much detail as I imagined.

05:28.250 --> 05:31.040
That's her official history, at least.

05:31.330 --> 05:35.580
Official? Is this about... the online backlash?

05:36.170 --> 05:40.080
No, I don't know the details behind that incident, actually.

05:40.710 --> 05:41.580
I see.

05:42.040 --> 05:43.670
What I mean by her nonofficial side...

05:45.790 --> 05:47.880
Have you ever heard of "LookIdiot"?

05:50.170 --> 05:54.080
Everyone knows pop idols aren't supposed
to smoke or have boyfriends, right?

05:54.420 --> 05:57.710
That's why I think it's their own fault they're
getting exposed like this.

05:56.830 --> 05:57.710
What is this?

05:57.710 --> 06:02.670
<b>[Leaked] Rainbow Girls Caught Smoking
Take a Look at Reality, Idiot</b>

05:58.000 --> 06:01.630
It's an account that suddenly appeared
about three years ago.

06:01.630 --> 06:05.830
It started revealing a string of scandals along with proof.

06:02.710 --> 06:05.790
<b>Take a Look at Reality, Idiot</b>

06:02.710 --> 06:05.790
<b>A channel with 23K followers and 15 videos
We reveal the truth behind rumors and the ugly reality of the show biz industry/idols</b>

06:06.130 --> 06:11.790
And well, there was speculation that the person behind
this account was actually Nono-tan's mother, Ms. Yukine.

06:13.830 --> 06:15.790
<b>[Leaked] Rainbow Girls Caught Smoking</b>

06:13.830 --> 06:15.790
<b>The group has been pulled from the Summer Festival lineup
The Sunflower Dolls get big break in their place</b>

06:15.330 --> 06:18.630
"The Sunflower Dolls get big break in their place."

06:19.380 --> 06:22.330
In order for an independent production company to
stand up to industry pressure,

06:22.330 --> 06:24.250
they think this must have been the only way.

06:25.580 --> 06:28.170
Oh. But they stopped posting quite a while ago.

06:28.170 --> 06:30.960
Yes. The month when Nono-tan got bashed online

06:30.960 --> 06:34.210
and the Sundolls went on hiatus was
when the account ceased activity.

06:35.420 --> 06:40.130
The truth remains unknown,
but this is what the fans say...

06:40.130 --> 06:41.580
<b>Is this girl Yoru Umitsuki from JELEE
who everyone's talking about?!</b>

06:42.250 --> 06:48.630
Yukine Hayakawa holds the keys
to the gates of both heaven and hell.

06:58.580 --> 06:59.540
Wow.

07:01.290 --> 07:02.750
<b>Kano
Yamanouchi</b>

07:02.960 --> 07:03.920
Aaack?!

07:04.250 --> 07:05.920
I checked out your rough draft!

07:05.920 --> 07:06.670
Oh!

07:07.790 --> 07:08.790
Sorry, about that-

07:08.790 --> 07:11.460
It's amazing, as usual!

07:11.670 --> 07:13.790
Huh? R-really?

07:14.080 --> 07:17.580
But I sent it even though the arm looks skewed.

07:17.580 --> 07:22.710
No problem! The appeal of your art isn't diminished
even if it's a tiny bit skewed.

07:24.290 --> 07:25.710
You're being too nice.

07:25.920 --> 07:33.580
It's true! You said I was the leader,
but you should know I really rely on you, Mahiru.

07:36.380 --> 07:41.000
Uh hey, Kano. There's something I need to tell you.

07:41.500 --> 07:43.710
Huh? What's this all of a sudden?

07:44.330 --> 07:46.210
Ms. Yukine Hayakawa...

07:47.290 --> 07:48.040
Huh?

07:49.210 --> 07:55.080
Your mother. She... contacted me with
a request to commission my art.

07:56.830 --> 07:59.210
A job for the Sundolls, you mean?

08:00.000 --> 08:03.170
For a promotional event at the end of the year.

08:04.710 --> 08:07.130
I haven't responded yet.

08:07.460 --> 08:12.040
But if I'm going to do it, it might affect
my work on our next music video.

08:14.250 --> 08:16.540
Do you want to do it, Mahiru?

08:18.250 --> 08:19.500
I'm conflicted.

08:19.830 --> 08:22.380
But part of me wants to take on the challenge.

08:22.380 --> 08:24.000
I can't say I'd recommend it.

08:26.880 --> 08:31.330
Hey, about you and your mom.
What happened between you two?

08:33.290 --> 08:36.630
Oops, sorry! This isn't something
I should spring on you over the phone.

08:36.920 --> 08:40.580
Um, if you ever want to talk about it in person is fine.

08:41.460 --> 08:43.420
All right, yeah.

08:43.670 --> 08:48.170
I'm going to go hear about the details on the weekend
but it wouldn't be right to go without telling you,

08:48.170 --> 08:49.580
so I wanted you to know.

08:50.080 --> 08:51.040
That's all!

08:52.920 --> 08:53.880
You're gonna go meet her.

08:53.880 --> 08:54.540
Huh?

08:54.880 --> 08:56.790
No, it's nothing.

08:57.420 --> 08:59.130
Thanks for telling me about it.

09:00.290 --> 09:01.080
Okay.

09:01.790 --> 09:03.670
Then I'll contact you again soon.

09:03.670 --> 09:05.330
Yeah. See you.

09:11.580 --> 09:12.880
Sorry for the wait.

09:19.790 --> 09:22.330
I'm the producer, Yukine Hayakawa.

09:26.790 --> 09:28.960
This is what you want me to do?

09:29.670 --> 09:32.330
It's a virtual live gig using a 3D avatar.

09:32.790 --> 09:34.580
We're coupling that with this.

09:35.580 --> 09:37.210
Projection mapping...

09:37.960 --> 09:40.790
You did something similar at your Halloween gig.

09:41.130 --> 09:44.750
But this event won't be at a music venue.

09:45.330 --> 09:47.710
The ground and all the buildings
at Miyashita Park in Shibuya

09:47.710 --> 09:49.920
will be covered with your art.

09:51.960 --> 09:54.380
In conjunction with the projection mapping images,

09:54.380 --> 09:57.540
a virtual version of the Sundolls
will dance at Miyashita Park.

09:58.040 --> 10:02.380
If this succeeds, this will go beyond
Japan and reach the world.

10:03.380 --> 10:08.960
So I want to put you in charge of the art for the
music video and the design for the virtual Sundolls.

10:09.170 --> 10:10.210
What do you think?

10:12.880 --> 10:14.710
Umm, can I ask a question?

10:14.960 --> 10:15.960
Of course.

10:16.920 --> 10:18.960
Why do you want me?

10:20.420 --> 10:21.710
What do you mean, why?

10:24.040 --> 10:28.290
This is such a big project! So why me?

10:29.250 --> 10:33.330
I just wondered... maybe because
I'm in the same group as Kano-!

10:33.330 --> 10:35.210
Oh, you mean Nonoka.

10:37.130 --> 10:38.580
This has absolutely nothing to do with her.

10:39.210 --> 10:41.920
I got inspired when I was watching your gig.

10:44.500 --> 10:47.380
Your drawing at the end was incredible.

10:49.710 --> 10:55.630
It gave me amazing inspiration,
and that's why I want your art.

10:56.460 --> 11:00.130
But my art is still really underdeveloped.

11:02.750 --> 11:03.790
True.

11:04.330 --> 11:06.380
For example, this most recent rough draft...

11:07.330 --> 11:08.710
It's a little skewed.

11:10.790 --> 11:14.580
U-um, that was bothering me as well, actually.

11:14.580 --> 11:16.130
There's an updated version I fixed!

11:16.670 --> 11:17.630
Really?

11:20.920 --> 11:23.630
I never doubted my eye for talent.

11:23.630 --> 11:24.250
Huh?

11:25.130 --> 11:29.000
Your art style hasn't changed,
but your drawing skills are obviously improving.

11:30.000 --> 11:33.250
You're practicing the basics properly, aren't you?

11:35.790 --> 11:38.750
I started attending a class this year,

11:39.080 --> 11:41.880
and I've been doing a ton of sketch studies recently.

11:42.170 --> 11:45.500
Ah. Well, the results speak for themselves.

11:47.000 --> 11:52.380
If you work with me, I promise you
your art will shine even more.

11:53.250 --> 11:57.290
So I'm asking the artist Yoru Umitsuki.
Won't you think about doing this together?

12:00.250 --> 12:03.500
Good answer. I have high hopes for you.

12:11.960 --> 12:13.710
I'm still not sure about this.

12:14.130 --> 12:15.670
About joining the Sundolls?

12:16.040 --> 12:16.710
Yeah...

12:17.210 --> 12:18.210
You'll be fine.

12:18.790 --> 12:22.250
Oh, about the bangs.
Can you leave some weight to them?

12:22.670 --> 12:23.710
O-of course.

12:23.710 --> 12:26.670
You're a gifted singer after all, Kano.

12:27.380 --> 12:29.380
Me? Gifted?

12:29.880 --> 12:32.420
You have a voice that can move people's souls.

12:32.880 --> 12:34.710
That's a talent you were born with.

12:34.920 --> 12:36.380
R-really?

12:36.380 --> 12:38.670
Yes. I guarantee it.

12:40.000 --> 12:43.000
You think my singing will reach Dad, too?

12:44.210 --> 12:46.130
Well. I don't know about that.

12:49.330 --> 12:50.710
How does this look?

12:52.460 --> 12:54.000
It suits you well, Kano.

12:54.630 --> 12:56.670
No, starting today,

12:57.420 --> 12:59.420
you're Nonoka Tachibana.

13:02.580 --> 13:03.420
Wow...!

13:06.080 --> 13:07.040
Nonoka!

13:07.040 --> 13:09.250
You're singing is way too amazing!

13:09.710 --> 13:13.630
What a killer addition!
The new improved Sundolls will sell for sure!

13:14.040 --> 13:16.330
Hey, Yukine-pi? That part she just sang...

13:16.790 --> 13:20.540
Well, yes. It's the part you used to sing, as the center.

13:22.250 --> 13:23.040
Hey?

13:24.540 --> 13:27.790
Nonoka, is it true that you're Yukine-pi's daughter?

13:28.250 --> 13:29.710
Huh? Yeah.

13:30.670 --> 13:32.540
So it's true...

13:32.830 --> 13:34.000
What do you mean?

13:34.290 --> 13:37.500
Gee, sure wish I could've been born Yukine-pi's kid, too!

13:39.080 --> 13:40.170
It's fine.

13:40.630 --> 13:42.460
Just silence them with your talent.

13:43.040 --> 13:46.040
But it's my first day and they hate me already.

13:46.040 --> 13:48.290
Talent always invites jealousy, doesn't it?

13:49.460 --> 13:52.710
I've never made any friends at school, either.

13:53.210 --> 13:55.670
Do you think I'm weird or something?

13:57.580 --> 14:00.380
Did I ever tell you that I have a dream?

14:01.040 --> 14:01.790
Huh?

14:02.330 --> 14:07.630
I want to one day nurture an artist who
sings to an audience of 50,000 people.

14:08.380 --> 14:10.960
50,000 people? Why?

14:11.130 --> 14:12.460
The number of seats at Tokyo Dome.

14:14.040 --> 14:19.630
With an artist I nurture from scratch, I want to deliver the
best possible entertainment to 50,000 people at once.

14:20.170 --> 14:23.830
Compared to that, being weird is a trivial concern, isn't it?

14:24.790 --> 14:29.130
So Nonoka, if you're lost as to what you're singing for,

14:29.540 --> 14:31.670
won't you sing for my sake?

14:35.880 --> 14:36.580
Sure!

14:41.790 --> 14:42.790
This sounds great.

14:43.250 --> 14:47.130
Ms. Yukine, I think this group might
just make it all the way.

14:47.460 --> 14:49.580
Of course. That's what I intend.

14:49.830 --> 14:53.460
<b>One
year</b>

14:49.840 --> 14:53.460
<b>later...</b>

14:52.130 --> 14:53.500
The final act at Summerfest?!

14:53.750 --> 14:56.750
Yes. I managed to get us in
a spot that suddenly opened up.

14:57.000 --> 14:59.500
But when you say "suddenly opened up"...

15:00.000 --> 15:01.170
You don't mean...

15:01.170 --> 15:03.380
<b>Rainbow Girls on Hiatus Over
Leaked Smoking Video</b>

15:03.540 --> 15:06.420
My Yukine-pi's such a boss at her job!

15:07.380 --> 15:10.420
I'm not sure I'm happy about this.

15:13.040 --> 15:14.750
<b>Rainbow Girls
Mugita
My life has lost all meaning</b>

15:13.040 --> 15:14.750
<b>#RainbowGirls</b>

15:13.040 --> 15:14.750
<b>Patuan</b>

15:13.050 --> 15:14.750
<b>What am I supposed to look forward to
in life starting tomorrow?</b>

15:13.050 --> 15:14.750
<b>#RainbowGirls</b>

15:15.330 --> 15:16.920
<b>Mugita
My life has lost all meaning</b>

15:15.340 --> 15:16.920
<b>#RainbowGirls</b>

15:15.340 --> 15:16.920
<b>Patuan
What am I supposed to look forward
to in life starting tomorrow?</b>

15:15.340 --> 15:16.920
<b>#RainbowGirls</b>

15:16.920 --> 15:18.790
<b>Nekonoyama
I need to lie down now</b>

15:16.920 --> 15:18.790
<b>#RainbowGirls</b>

15:16.920 --> 15:18.790
<b>Vagabond Type A
This can't be happening...right...???</b>

15:16.920 --> 15:18.790
<b>#RainbowGirls</b>

15:16.920 --> 15:18.790
<b>Power Kid
What... Why...?</b>

15:16.920 --> 15:18.790
<b>#RainbowGirls</b>

15:21.830 --> 15:24.830
On behalf of all the Rainbow Girls, I cannot...

15:25.540 --> 15:26.790
apologize enough...

15:28.420 --> 15:30.960
Yeah, the account's called "LookIdiot."

15:30.960 --> 15:34.540
But I don't think it's right for us to get our big
break that way.

15:35.540 --> 15:36.540
Oh, yeah!

15:36.540 --> 15:41.080
They're letting me write some lyrics soon, but it's so hard.

15:41.630 --> 15:44.130
Hey, what do you think I should write about?

15:44.750 --> 15:46.080
Thanks for today!

15:46.630 --> 15:48.170
It made me super happy.

15:48.710 --> 15:51.080
I feel like I haven't been called Kano in ages.

15:51.630 --> 15:52.750
But whatever.

15:53.250 --> 15:54.040
So...

15:54.750 --> 15:56.040
Anyway I'll see you,

15:56.040 --> 15:57.000
Dad!

15:57.830 --> 16:00.210
Yeah. See you again, Kano.

16:09.460 --> 16:10.630
What weird colors.

16:14.540 --> 16:15.880
Such weird colors!

16:18.130 --> 16:21.080
"Sparkling you swim, you're just beautiful."

16:22.170 --> 16:25.460
"I'm hidden behind these jet black bangs..."

16:32.790 --> 16:34.750
<b>jellyfish
sea moon</b>

16:36.420 --> 16:39.420
The kanji characters for jellyfish are "sea moon."

16:39.710 --> 16:41.080
"Lit by the colorful moonlight,"

16:41.080 --> 16:42.420
"I got to meet you that night in Shibuya."

16:45.040 --> 16:53.380
<b>A gift from the Watase Atelier of Painting
Original idea by</b>

16:45.460 --> 16:48.460
"I don't even know who you are,

16:48.880 --> 16:53.380
<b>Yoru Umitsuki</b>

16:49.250 --> 16:51.380
...with that radiance

16:49.920 --> 16:51.500
but I... fell in love."

16:51.380 --> 16:56.040
Don't get washed over by the urban neon, and please

16:55.330 --> 16:56.460
Mahiru...

16:56.040 --> 17:03.750
Sparkle with the colors you paint and light up the night sky

17:01.040 --> 17:03.500
I don't have to worry... right?

17:03.750 --> 17:04.830
So that someday I can...

17:10.380 --> 17:12.380
Huh? This phone.

17:13.580 --> 17:14.540
It's Mero's.

